.TH RESGUARDCTL 1 "November 2026" "resguard" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
resguardctl \- query the resguard resource monitor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B resguardctl
.RB [ \-socket
.IR path ]
.RI [ command " [" arguments ...]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B resguardctl
talks to the
.BR resguardd (8)
daemon to show the system state, the resource usage of every service,
application and container, and the recorded incidents (resource peaks, OOM
kills and service failures).
.PP
Without a
.I command
it opens an interactive session with history (up and down arrows) and
completion (Tab). With a
.I command
it runs it and exits.
.PP
To use it without
.BR sudo ,
the user must belong to the
.B resguard
group:
.B sudo usermod \-aG resguard $USER
and log in again.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Summary: CPU, memory, swap, load, pressure (PSI) and incidents in the last hour.
.TP
.BR watch " [" \fIseconds\fR ]
Full-screen live view. Keys: arrows to select a row,
.B Enter
to see its processes,
.BR a / s / d / t
to show only applications, services, containers or everything,
.BR c / m
to sort by CPU or memory,
.B Esc
to go back and
.B q
to quit.
.TP
.BR services " [" cpu | mem "] [" apps | services | containers | sessions "] [" \fIn\fR ]
What uses the most resources, with its kind, memory limit and OOM kills.
.TP
.BR history " [" \fIn\fR ]
The last \fIn\fR samples (20 by default).
.TP
.BR events " [" \fIn\fR ]
The last \fIn\fR incidents (20 by default).
.TP
.BI event " id"
Details of an incident, with the system state and what used the most resources.
.TP
.BR logs " [" \fIn\fR "] [" warnings "] [" follow ]
Service logs from the journal: the last \fIn\fR lines, warnings and errors
only, or live (Ctrl+C goes back). The daemon's logs are always in English.
.TP
.B config
Configuration in use and the file it was loaded from.
.TP
.BR ping ", " version ", " help
Utilities.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-socket " path"
Daemon socket (default
.IR /run/resguard/resguard.sock ).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RESGUARD_LANG
CLI language:
.B en
or
.BR es .
When unset, the system language is used
.RB ( LANG ", " LC_MESSAGES ", " LANGUAGE );
any language other than Spanish falls back to English.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set, output uses no colors.
.TP
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
Directory of the command history (default
.IR ~/.local/state ).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/resguard/history
Interactive mode history (readable only by the user). Lines starting with a
space are not saved.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B resguardctl services apps mem
Applications using the most memory.
.TP
.B resguardctl logs warnings follow
Peaks, OOM kills and failures as they happen.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR resguardd (8),
.BR journalctl (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
